<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sinking of the Rainbow Warrior</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1985">1985</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Rainbow Warrior bombing, Opération Satanique</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The sinking of the Rainbow Warrior was a bombing by agents of the French foreign intelligence service, the DGSE, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auckland">Auckland</a> harbour on 10 July 1985. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greenpeace">Greenpeace</a> ship was preparing to protest against French nuclear tests at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moruroa">Moruroa</a>, and the photographer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fernando-pereira">Fernando Pereira</a> was killed. Two agents were convicted in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, and the affair forced the French defence minister to resign and caused a lasting breach between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and New Zealand.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sinking-of-the-rainbow-warrior.jpg" alt="Sinking of the Rainbow Warrior" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ot · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RainbowWarrior-1985b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
